    "goal": "Make a discarded run's departure read discarded in the fleet transitions, distinct from withdrawn, by having discard() in reckon/crew/promotion.py (near line 4558) write a discard record into the run directory, carrying the discard time, before it removes the live pointer, and by having the departure rule in reckon/crew/recovery.py (near line 5167, which today yields promoted when the ledger records the run and withdrawn otherwise) read that record as discarded. reckon-ee observed at 11:14:53 on 2026-09-26 that a crew discard rendered complete to withdrawn, so a reader cannot tell a deliberate discard from a pointer that vanished. Any renderer that styles departure states must accept discarded. A promotion recorded in the ledger still reads promoted, whatever else the run directory holds.",
